# EVA - build-time tooling (NOT part of the runtime dependency set).
# Compiled into requirements-build.lock; build/scripts/build-backend.ps1 installs
# requirements.lock + requirements-build.lock into a fresh Python 3.11 venv.
#
# The constraint (-c requirements.lock) keeps packages shared with the runtime
# set (setuptools, packaging) at the runtime lock's versions, so the two files
# install together without a version conflict.
#
# Regenerate after editing this file (or after re-locking requirements.lock):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-build.in -o requirements-build.lock --universal \
#       --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes -c requirements.lock
